+# Native need association V3: exact requested and adapted commands
+
+V2's single seed 2026111301 completed 12 decisions and stored no source records.
+Seven Rest and three Inspect selections failed the coarse binding gate; two
+locomotion representatives were unsupported. There were no changed logits or
+paired recalls. That life and its source, executable, plan and result remain
+preserved. It is never retried, extended or counted as evidence of competence.
+
+A concrete source defect was found independently of that outcome: the world
+receives the selected channel command, adapts its intensity through actual body
+capability, then stores the adapted command in its physical receipt. V2 compared
+that receipt against the unadapted command. Its journal did not record the exact
+failed subpredicate, so this diagnosis is not retrospective proof that it was
+the only reason for the recorded null.
+
+V3 shares PreparedMotorChannelAdapter with canonical world execution. It prepares
+the same embodiment and locomotor capacity once from the actual pre-action
+record. Both world execution and admission call the unchanged adaptation
+function. The gate checks the requested representative command against the
+selected neural command and separately checks every adapted command against its
+own physical receipt. Channel, primitive, target, payload, timing and all other
+fields remain exact. Real movement is not accepted as a no-op merely because
+its force or displacement is zero. Unsupported locomotion representatives remain
+unsupported. V3 changes neither world physiology nor actuator semantics.
+
+The private port has a new identity, cpu-stationary-own-history-advantage-v3.
+No acquired V1 store, default foundation, old checkpoint or production brain is
+reinterpreted. The core circuit, engineered weights, reference, normalization,
+work charge, support domain and limits are unchanged. Failed binding diagnostics
+now identify the exact first predicate instead of one combined label. Actual
+measured before-state must match the native record and world receipt. Measured
+after-state must match the final once-charged host state, not the earlier world
+after-state; tests reject omitted and duplicated charge.
+
+At this source checkpoint, no V3 native life has run. The used V2 executable life
+entry point is deliberately absent. Focused physical-receipt and biology tests
+are synthetic boundary tests, not native selection envelopes or acquired records.
+A fresh admission protocol will be separately frozen before any actual life.
+
+## Prospective fresh admission
+
+A new no-retry fixture uses sampling seed 2026111302, fixed construction/world
+seed 2026111301 and the exact same inherited asset SHA-256
+1d2978cbd857a7ca99dc1b2cf65be9f6ff417a6f78199282e0431b94332c9377. The scan of
+available public protocols found no use of sampling 2026111302; the seed is
+explicitly reserved with the parent. This is a bounded check, not a global
+uniqueness claim. The scene, prior, 12-decision budget, health/reserve stops,
+reference, pressure quantum and work charging match V2. Native moves remain
+available; records and context are never manually seeded or reset.
+
+The single V3 entry point has a distinct name, study identity and output path.
+A create-new marker precedes its first native decision. A null, failed or stopped
+life is not replaced or extended. The local journal includes requested commands,
+actual adapted commands, each physical channel receipt and explicit before/after
+biology equality checks. These are fresh diagnostic records, not restoration
+state or publishable raw journals. Only bounded, reviewed summaries are shared.
